<title>USA: Toys R Us Inc Q4 net rose. [CORRECTED 17:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Toys R Us Inc Q4 net rose. [CORRECTED 17:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARAMUS, N.J. 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.37		    $0.34</p>
<p> Net			382,900		   93,000</p>
<p> Revs		   4,667,500		4,605,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 279,200		  274,200</p>
<p>Year</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.54		    $0.53</p>
<p> Net			427,400		  148,100</p>
<p> Revs		   9,932,400		9,426,900</p>
<p>(Corrects year-ago figure from 4,426,900 to 9,426,900)</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 277,500		  276,900</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: First Call concensus for Q4 was $1.42/shr.</p>
<p>1997 net includes pretax charges of $4.5 million in qtr and $59.5 million in year relating toarbitration award against the company. These are equal to $2.8 million and $37.5 million, respectively, after taxes and reduced per share net from $1.38 and $1.68, respectively.</p>
<p>1996 net in both periods includes pretax restructuring charge of $396.6 million, equal to $269.1 million after taxes which reduced per share net from $1.32 in quarter and $1.51 in year.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
